@bank all
// SW6 (ending writer A), the goodbye (ending spec, "If you go", Monday Day 36; section 9: content/ending/goodbye.lines).
// Scenes beside this file: endingBreakfast (the last breakfast) and endingRamp (Zeke at the ramp's foot, last). Here:
// the morning's notices and Tracked rows, the breakfast bubbles, the aisle (a ring on each person as you pass; one
// press each; their lines in order, card lines, 90 at most), and the crowd's calls (bubbles, 60 at most).
// The order in the aisle: each close friend in turn, then Calder, Vance, the Captain; Zeke last at the ramp.
// Only with flag:end.go. Nobody says "leave" about the reach; you're going to Concord headquarters.

// ---- the last morning: notices and Tracked rows (EN1)
== ending.notice.lastMorning
- Your last morning: the Tern leaves at 10:00.
== ending.status.lastMorning
- Today 10:00: the Tern leaves for the Concord courier.
== ending.tracked.breakfast
- Breakfast in the mess, your last one
== ending.tracked.bay
- The shuttle bay by 09:30
== ending.tracked.ramp
- Walk to the Tern
== ending.ring.walk
- Walk to the Tern
// your cabin's things packed (the cabin touches boxed: their tap texts)
== ending.tap.boxed
- Packed and labelled. The label says "Wren" and then, in smaller writing, "headquarters".
- Boxed up. It takes less room than it did on the shelf. It took more room than this in you.   #warm
- Your keepsakes, wrapped in a Works orange scarf. Far too long. Perfect for wrapping.   #warm

// ---- Monday's fetches (EN1, RV21's review): bubbles, 60 at most. Pell at 08:30 if you're not at breakfast; Zeke at
// 10:15 if you're not in the shuttle bay
== ending.breakfast.fetch
- There you are! Breakfast. Brennan's holding your plate.   #funny
== ending.bay.fetch
- There you are. Half the ship's in the bay. With me.   #warm
// the "Goodbye" button on a farewell's card in the bay
== ending.btn.bye
- Goodbye

// ---- breakfast: bubbles at the tables (60 at most)
== ending.breakfast.here
- Last breakfast. Eat slowly. Make it last.   #warm
- Nobody's taking the seat by you. We decided.   #warm
- Brennan's been up since four. For you.   #warm
- I can't eat. I'm eating. I can't.   #funny
- Half nine, the bay. The whole shift's going.
- Day shift's let off at half nine. All of it. For you.   #warm

// ---- the aisle: each close friend's goodbye as you pass (a ring, one press; lines in order).
== ending.goodbye.pell.1
- Oi oi. Last time I'll say that to your face. Here. From the tin.
== ending.goodbye.pell.2
- A screw from the Wren. Every ship gets one. Start your own tin, spanner.   #warm
== ending.goodbye.pell.3
- Right. Go on. Before I do something embarrassing. I'm doing it anyway.   #funny
== ending.goodbye.tomas.1
- I've marked you on the map. Under the Wren. "Bunkmate." In pencil.   #warm
== ending.goodbye.tomas.2
- I'll write every week. I'll make it sound more exciting than it is.   #funny
== ending.goodbye.tomas.3
- Thank you for being new with me. That's all. Thank you.   #warm
== ending.goodbye.kovac-zainab.1
- Oh. Hi. Here. It's a scarf. A short one. To go with his long one.   #warm
== ending.goodbye.kovac-zainab.2
- It's perfect. I counted every stitch. Twice. Bye, then.   #warm
== ending.goodbye.bramwell-basil.1
- You can't go, you're my mentor. Sorry. I know. I practised not saying that.   #funny
== ending.goodbye.bramwell-basil.2
- The plant's doing better. I wanted you to know. It's got a new leaf. Look.   #warm
== ending.goodbye.bramwell-basil.3
- I'll be you for the next new one. Is that all right? I'll try. Brilliant. Bye!   #warm
== ending.goodbye.halloran-emeka.1
- Ah, look at you. There's a scone in your bag. Two. I'm not saying which pocket.   #warm
== ending.goodbye.halloran-emeka.2
- Your mug stays on the rack. It doesn't come down. That's the rule. Look after yourself.   #warm
== ending.goodbye.rina.1
- I've told the Tern's medic you need sleep and breakfast. They took notes.   #funny
== ending.goodbye.rina.2
- I'm still undefeated. Come back and fix that. That's an order. Medical.   #warm
== ending.goodbye.brennan.1
- Oh, love. Here. A tin of biscuits for the trip. Share them. Don't share them.   #warm
== ending.goodbye.brennan.2
- Your page stays in my book. Your dish stays on my menu. Go on. Eat something there.   #warm
// a close friend without their own lines (the engine fills {hi}, {nick} and the rest from their voice card)
== ending.goodbye.friend
- {hi}, {nick}. This is me not crying. Look after yourself. Write.   #warm
- {bye}, {nick}. The Wren's better for you having been on her.   #warm
- Go on, then. Go and be brilliant. We'll tell everyone we knew you first.   #warm
- {thanks}. For all of it. You know what I mean. Off you go.   #warm
- I brought you nothing, because you'd have to carry it. I brought me. Bye.   #funny
// a friend (not close) in the aisle, a wave as you pass (bubble, 60)
== ending.goodbye.wave
- Good luck up there!
- Write to us!
- Mind the step at headquarters!   #funny
- Safe trip, {nick}.   #warm
- Come back and visit!   #warm

// ---- Calder, then Vance, then the Captain (in that order, after the friends)
== ending.goodbye.calder.1
- I'm checking the ramp seals.
== ending.goodbye.calder.2
- That's a lie. They're fine. I came for you.
== ending.goodbye.calder.3
- I keep a list of every tech I've certified. A note by each. Yours says "Good." Underlined.   #warm
== ending.goodbye.calder.4
- Nobody thanks the air. That's how you know it's working. You worked. Go on.   #warm
== ending.goodbye.vance.1
- Cadet. Regulation forty: crew departing are seen off by the duty officer. That's me.   #funny
== ending.goodbye.vance.2
- There is no regulation forty. I wanted to come. Your name's on my list. The good one.   #warm
== ending.goodbye.vance.3
- My rowing pin. Lent, not given. You'll have to bring it back one day. Carry on.   #warm
== ending.goodbye.marrow.1
- {me}. You answered my question, your first week. I still have it written down.   #warm
== ending.goodbye.marrow.2
- The Admiral asked me to see you off. He's bad at goodbyes. He's sulking in the ready room.   #funny
== ending.goodbye.marrow.3
- There's always a place for you on the Wren. Mind the step at headquarters. Everyone trips.   #warm

// ---- the crowd (about 60 in the bay; bubbles, 60 at most) as you walk the aisle, and the cheer as you go up
== ending.goodbye.crowd
- There they go!
- Good luck, {me}!
- Three cheers on the ramp! Wait for it!
- Who's crying? Nobody. Everyone.   #funny
- Headquarters won't know what's hit them.   #funny
- Best five weeks, that was.   #warm
- Don't forget us!
- Mind the step!   #funny
- Wave! They're waving! Wave back!
- I only met them once. I'm still crying.   #funny
== ending.goodbye.crowd.cheer
- Hip, hip!
- Hooray!
- To {me}!
- Safe trip!   #warm
